<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><title>Delete account - bitcoin++</title>{{ block "header" . }}{{ end }}{{ template "admin_favicon" "" }}</head>
<body class="btcpp-admin-page bg-gray-50 text-gray-900">{{ block "mainnav" . }}{{ end }}
<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-8"><a href="/admin/people" class="text-indigo-600">← People and identities</a>
<h1 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Delete account</h1>
{{ if .Error }}<p role="alert" class="my-4 rounded border border-red-300 bg-red-50 p-4">{{ .Error }}</p>{{ end }}
<section class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-white p-6 shadow"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">{{ .Preview.Name }}</h2><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs">{{ .Preview.ID }}</p>{{ range .Preview.Emails }}<p class="text-sm">{{ . }}</p>{{ end }}
<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">History that will remain</h3><ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 text-sm"><li>{{ .Preview.Talks }} talk proposals</li><li>{{ .Preview.Projects }} hackathon projects</li><li>{{ .Preview.Judging }} judging scorecards</li><li>{{ .Preview.Registrations }} linked registrations (contact details removed and tickets revoked)</li></ul>
<p class="mt-4 text-sm">Talks, projects, and judging records will be attributed to a new anonymous profile with a random alias such as “anon03910”. Project ownership passes to the longest-standing remaining teammate, or stays under admin management if none remain. Shared talk notes are retained; shared invitation links are replaced to invalidate the old links. This profile cannot sign in or receive account credentials.</p>
<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">Data that will be removed</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm">The original profile, email aliases, login credentials, roles, organization access, and associated merge recovery snapshots. Linked contact information is removed from registrations, volunteer records, and shop orders. Financial totals, historical attendance totals, and award history remain.</p>
<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">External data needs a separate review</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm">This deletes account data in this application's database. Previously sent or queued emails in the mail service, object-storage uploads (including portraits and tax forms), payment and shipping provider records, logs, backups, published PDFs, and recordings are separate. Names embedded in talk descriptions, project content, or editorial reports are not automatically rewritten. Review those as part of the speaker's request.</p>
<form method="post" action="/admin/people/delete" class="mt-6 border-t pt-6"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{ .CSRF }}"><input type="hidden" name="person" value="{{ .Preview.ID }}">
<label class="block text-sm font-semibold" for="delete-confirmation">Type DELETE to confirm</label><input id="delete-confirmation" name="confirmation" required pattern="DELETE" autocomplete="off" class="mt-2 rounded border px-3 py-2">
<label class="mt-4 flex gap-2 text-sm"><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_delete" value="yes" required>I have verified the account owner's request and understand that this deletion cannot be undone.</label>
<button type="submit" class="mt-6 rounded bg-red-700 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-white">Permanently delete account</button></form></section></main></body></html>
